<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="section">
    <div class="container-narrow">
        <div class="section-header">
            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border);">
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>What does a foot massager do?</h3>
                <p>A foot massager uses a combination of kneading, air compression, vibration, and heat to deliver targeted comfort to your feet and, in some models, your calves and ankles. It is designed for daily home use as part of a simple relaxation or recovery routine.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Is a heated foot massager better?</h3>
                <p>Heat enhances the overall comfort of the massage by helping muscles feel more relaxed. Most buyers find that a heated foot massager delivers a more complete, soothing experience compared to models without heat.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>What is the difference between a foot massager and a foot and calf massager?</h3>
                <p>A foot massager focuses on the soles, arches, and ankles. A foot and calf massager extends the massage up to the lower legs, which is especially helpful for people who stand for long periods or experience lower-leg stiffness.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Are foot massagers good for tired feet?</h3>
                <p>A foot massager for tired feet can provide meaningful comfort after a long day. The combination of heat and kneading helps your feet feel lighter and more relaxed, making it easier to wind down in the evening.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Can I use a foot massager every day?</h3>
                <p>Most foot massagers are designed for daily use. Short, consistent sessions tend to be more effective than occasional long sessions. Start with 15 minutes and adjust based on comfort.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Is a foot massager a good gift?</h3>
                <p>Foot massagers are one of the most popular and practical wellness gifts. They work for almost anyone — parents, partners, or anyone who appreciates daily comfort and self-care at home.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Can I try foot massagers before buying?</h3>
                <p>Yes. You can visit the Massage Chairs and More showroom to test foot massagers and other wellness products in person. It is the easiest way to compare models and find the right fit before you buy.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

